From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:04:59 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform-segacd

Sega CD / Mega-CD gets one shelf, Games/SEGACD, on the Genesis Plus GX
that already plays the Mega Drive. Platform::SegaCd is appended to
SHELVES; Core::EVERY and upstream's ALL lists stay as they are. Discs
are .chd, .cue, .iso and .m3u files (a .bin is a track, never a game,
the PS1 rule), titled by their stem without a (Disc N) tag. Every
policy method answers Sega CD explicitly and the same as the Mega Drive:
the 6-button pad on X, Y, L and R, slot keeps L2 and R2, no core
picker, Stretch follows the live frame width, rewind on. The 320x224
picture uses the Mega Drive's 360x240 canvas. Its shader is stored in
Config/segacd_shader.txt and offers the retro list. Saves/SEGACD,
States/SEGACD and Labels/SEGACD are made at boot. The release year
order puts it after the SNES (Mega-CD, Japan, 12 December 1991).

Only for a Sega CD disc slot answers genesis_plus_gx_system_bram with
per game, so each game keeps its own <stem>.brm, and
genesis_plus_gx_cd_precache with disabled, so a reload reads only the
CHD's header. genesis_plus_gx_cart_size stays unanswered: the pinned
core stores "disabled" as 0xff, which mounts a cart with a mask of 1 <<
268, while an unanswered option leaves it at 0, no cart. The Mega Drive,
Master System and Game Gear get no new option. The shelf shows the
jewel case of patch segacd-carts.
